{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pulls/158","id":4744808174,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTEdTLM8AAAABGtAG7g","html_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/158","diff_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/158.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/158.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/issues/158","number":158,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Revalidate Orabona Theorem 2.7 and qualify shared first-order reader","user":{"login":"jicheng9617","id":74550583,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NTUwNTgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74550583?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617","html_url":"https://github.com/jicheng9617","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The supporting-gradient reader conflated the extended-real Theorem 2.7, its two library helpers and the stronger historical OGD regularity interface. This package revalidates the three retained proofs with distinct semantic actors and qualifies only the existing first-order reader; all statement hashes, proof tokens and canary bytes remain unchanged. No new proofs or registry nodes are claimed.\n\nThe terminal retains global noBottom, ambient interior, the derivative of canonical F(z)=(f(z)).toReal justified by a proved local embedding identity, and every comparator including positive infinity outside the domain. The everywhere-real ConvexOn helper needs x/y membership and an ambient derivative at x; it does not require open V or the extended-real bridge. Historical RegularLoss OGD and the separate source-compatible adapter are explicitly distinguished.\n\nValidation: fresh shared root (9088 jobs), Tests (9230 jobs), complete harness (466 tests, 7 existing skips), 12 named axiom audits, 3 native guards, byte-identical nondegenerate canary, exact stacked contributor gate (4 production paths/1 manifest), scoped whitespace, clean lean-verified site/check, 3 canonical nodes and all 10806 old IDs/URLs retained. The actual compiled graph export is scoped to 3 nodes/416 direct edges, not a full/canary graph. Distinct contract/body/final reader decisions and exact historical snapshot bindings are recorded.\n\nStacked dependency: OPEN draft #157 at a6607d8213860619965c7018e4dd2effff58422a; this is not accepted on main. The main-relative contributor diagnostic still reports 15 other legacy module contracts missing. Full whitespace diagnostic fails on exact raw logs; scoped checking preserves those enumerated raw bytes and checks code/JSON/scripts/docs. Chapter 2 has an incomplete/null mandatory total and Chapters 1–16 Goal remains active; legacy semantic migrations decrease only 19→18. No merge or deployment.\n\nEvidence: runs/online-first-order-migration-20261005/accepted-decision-v1.json, accepted-binding-audit-v1.json, native-acceptance-overlay-v1.json, final-reader-receipt-v1.json, integrated-gates-overlay-v1.json; frozen source/native targets in docs/contracts/online-first-order-migration-v1. Site source commit 63453e28ae0ce86a87c6cc1b11ef0403bfe0141c is distinct from later evidence/delivery commits.\n","created_at":"2026-10-05T12:20:42Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T12:20:42Z","clos